// Test for builtin_tools/plan_tool.h (namespace kimix::builtin_tools::plan).
//
// Two layers:
//
// 1. Kernel unit tests with hand-written expectations (parameters, the render
//    engines, the char window, the edit chain, the message builders, the Tool
//    wrappers).
// 2. Golden replay (tests/unit/builtin_tools/plan_goldens.inc), regenerated by
//    `python scripts/gen_plan_goldens.py` from the REAL Python implementation
//    in the kimi-agent checkout (src/kimix/tools/note/__init__.py), driven
//    through `CallableTool2.call` exactly like the agent toolset:
//      * kPlanMeta            - LLM-facing description + pydantic parameter
//                               schema (compared structurally)
//      * kPlanParamGoldens    - which argument sets pydantic lets through
//      * kForwardGoldens / kTailGoldens - ReadPlan._read_forward/_read_tail
//                               (byte-exact output + message, plus the
//                               output byte/line counts for the corpora whose
//                               rendered output is too large to embed)
//      * kPlanWindowGoldens   - `output[char_offset:max_char]`
//      * kPlanToolGoldens     - end-to-end replay over real files: status,
//                               message, output, brief, the on-disk bytes and
//                               the ReadPlan render bookkeeping
//      * kPlanOsErrorGoldens  - OS-level failures (CPython's errno text is
//                               platform specific; the platform-independent
//                               parts are pinned)
//      * kPlanGateGoldens     - `_enable_plan` == False raises SkipThisTool
//
// All test logic lives in main() scope; no file-scope static registrations.
